{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1189"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge music-stage/theatre","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/zz-r2-music-stage__theatre.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",826],["+","These plays still find new forms on today's stages. The German piano cabaret artist Bodo Wartke turned Sophocles' “Oedipus Rex” into a humorous one-man show in rhyming verse: at its premiere at the Schmidt Theater in Hamburg on 17 May 2009 he played all fourteen roles himself, from the king to the oracle, and in 2018 he followed it with an “Antigone”.\n\n"],["=",109]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",802],["+","Diese Stücke finden auf heutigen Bühnen noch immer neue Formen. Der Klavierkabarettist Bodo Wartke machte aus Sophokles’ „König Ödipus“ ein humoristisches Ein-Mann-Stück in Reimen: Bei der Premiere am 17. Mai 2009 im Schmidt Theater in Hamburg spielte er alle vierzehn Rollen selbst, vom König bis zum Orakel, und 2018 ließ er eine „Antigone“ folgen.\n\n"],["=",109]]}]},
